// PORT-PENDING 1188 tests-web-dev-slice-1: tests/web_dev.rs:1-1586
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! c134 Phase 7: `jet dev <file>.jet --target=web` — the std-only watch +
//RS //! rebuild-on-save + live-reload dev server (Source/CmdDevWeb.rs). Starts the
//RS //! real `jet` binary as a child process, talks to it over a plain TCP socket
//RS //! (no new dependency — matches the server's own std-only HTTP), edits a
//RS //! throwaway temp copy of a fixture, and confirms the rebuild lands.
//RS //!
//RS //! Also covers c-devserver (owner-directed 2026-07-01): `jet dev <file>`
//RS //! when the file defines a top-level `fn dev()` — the file configures and
//RS //! starts its OWN `core.web.devserver` value instead of the CLI hardcoding
//RS //! `--target=web --port=<N>`. Same spawn/TCP/rebuild harness, driven through
//RS //! zero CLI flags — `jet dev app.jet`, no `--target=web`.
//RS 
